{"id": "EUVD-2026-103462", "enisaUuid": "264704c9-5919-3449-ac51-83ef28217246", "description": "smpeg through 2.0.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in MPEGsystem::FillBuffer() that allows attackers to read past the 16384-byte buffer by supplying a crafted system header stream table. Attackers can provide an MPEG file whose stream table bytes all set the high bit, which crashes applications opening it through SMPEG_new, SMPEG_new_rwops, or SMPEG_new_data.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:23:31", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/smpeg-system-header-stream-table-oob-read", "https://github.com/icculus/smpeg/blob/d188dc111f4817288718705e4a84e248803ccfdc/MPEGsystem.cpp#L803-L823", "https://github.com/icculus/smpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/smpeg-through-2.0.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-mpegsystem-fillbuffer"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hhc9-vxgx-6xvc", "CVE-2026-112009"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1eaa1793-dc9b-39e2-893c-6b592a43b4ab", "product": {"name": "smpeg", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aff9e95b-696c-3ec0-8059-8f55184e17c1", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}], "isExploited": false}